course: dictionary
lesson: 6100
title: Mew: a cry, a bird, a street
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Mew is a word with more than one meaning. Its main meaning is the soft, high cry a cat or kitten makes, and you can also mew as a verb. «Picture a kitten halfway up the curtains, mewing.» The word mewing shows the kitten is making that sound.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. «White storks are almost silent ... while chicks hiss and mew before they learn to clatter.» Chicks are baby birds, so mew here is a sound they make, not a street.
explain: Mews with an «s» can mean something different in the UK: a row of old stables in a city, now often turned into houses. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Mew means the soft, high cry of a cat or kitten, and it can also mean to make that cry.
fact: «Miaow» and «meow» are the usual words for a cat's sound, but mew is another word for it.
fact: A mew can also be the cry of a gull or other bird, especially the mew gull, a kind of seagull.
fact: In the UK, a mews is a row of old stables in a city, now often turned into houses, or a small street with such houses.
fact: Useful phrases: mew softly, and a mews house.
exercise: «Picture a kitten halfway up the curtains, mewing.» What is the kitten doing? | Sleeping in a warm box | Chasing a bird away | Running down the stairs | *Making a soft, high cry
exercise: In «chicks hiss and mew before they learn to clatter», what are the chicks doing? | Building a nest | *Making a soft cry | Flying away from the nest | Singing a long song
exercise: A child says, «We walked down the mews in London, past the little houses.» What is a mews? | A gull's cry over the sea | *A row of old stables turned into houses, or a small street with such houses | A kind of cat food | A sound a kitten makes
test: «The mew of a gull echoed over the harbour.» What does mew mean here? | A soft, high cry of a cat | A tiny boat | A row of old stables | *The cry of a seagull or other bird
test: Which word means a small street of houses in a city, made from old stables? | *Mews | Mew | Stable | Gull
exam: «Kittens mew when they are hungry.» What does mew mean in this sentence? | Stopping to rest | Hiding quietly under a bed | A sleepy yawn | *A soft, high cry that a kitten makes
